msgid "Analog Airspeed sensor would use :ref:`ARSPD_PIN<ARSPD_PIN>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:130
#: 84f6971791e54d5e84343d33b0325a8b
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:132
#: 9da284a286324ee1ad36aeed20725328
msgid "The TBS LUCID H7 does not have a builtin compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:135
#: f8a868593a1f437eacac9577a6c91c6c
msgid "VTX power control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:137
#: b28a3ad4d35d46dc99beca8718578bba
msgid "GPIO 81 controls the VSW pins which can be set to output either VBAT or 5V via a board jumper. Setting this GPIO high removes voltage supply to pins. RELAY2 is configured by default to control this GPIO and is low by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:139
#: c82775ace4ef4f3eb97b0c1674261404
msgid "GPIO 83 controls the VTX BEC output to pins marked \"9V\" and is included on the HD VTX connector. Setting this GPIO low removes voltage supply to this pin/pad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:141
#: 3253e17314994dbfad520cb7fd5426a2
msgid "By default RELAY4 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:144
#: 877172c35ec74906a8904a72c1f5c07e
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-lucidh7.rst:145
#: 50d3e628fdfb40e2ba81aaa65622a075
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the camera output to the connectors marked \"CAM1\" and \"CAM2\". Setting this GPIO low switches the video output from CAM1 to CAM2. By default RELAY3 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

